#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) ion acoustic wave (IAW) test.
A single-wavelength ion density perturbation is seeded along x in a uniform,
Maxwellian, zero-bulk-velocity proton plasma with a guide magnetic field along x
(k || B, so the wave is a clean longitudinal ion-acoustic mode).  The electric
field is initially zero; the restoring force is the electron pressure gradient
in the generalized Ohm's law (electronTemperature > 0, isothermal gamma = 1),
which gives the acoustic speed c_s = sqrt(Te/mi).

  n(x) = n0 * (1 + pert * sin(kx * x)),   kx = 2*pi*waveMode / Lx

The seed is implemented by the C++ TESTCASE IonAcousticWave, which scales each
particle's weight so the deposited ion density carries the sinusoidal profile
while keeping the bulk velocity uniform.

Parameters (modeled on tests/hybrid_whistler) put the ion scales at O(1) in
CODE (normalized) units: Lx = 6.4 d_i, d_i ~ 1, v_A ~ 1, B ~ Omega_i ~ 1.
With electronTemperature = 26 eV and uNorm = 5e4 m/s the acoustic speed is
c_s ~ 1, and with T = 1e4 K the ion thermal speed is v_thi ~ 0.26, so
c_s / v_thi ~ 4 (weak Landau damping: the wave oscillates and decays).

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
26.0                    electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Sub-cycle the B update: the explicit Hall advance is limited by the discrete
grid-scale modes, dt_sub < dx^2/(6 v_A d_i) ~ 1.7e-3 (dx = 0.1, v_A = d_i = 1),
so dt = 0.02 needs nHallSubcycle >= 12; 32 gives dt_sub = 6.25e-4 with margin.
#HALLSUBCYCLE
32                      nHallSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
1.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
5.2195e-9               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 along x (B_code ~ 1, k || B)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
IonAcousticWave
0.1                     pert       relative density-perturbation amplitude (< 1)
1                       waveMode   number of wavelengths across the x-domain

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
25                      dn
0.0                     dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez rhoS0  varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
25.0                    TimeMax

#RUN

#MOMENTTIMECENTERING
T                       useMomentTimeCentering

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB
